{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It shall not seem hard to you.</b> We find written 'for three years like the years of a hired worker,' and this is proof that a person has no authority to hire himself out for more than three years, likewise for the one who hires him who gives his wage." "And this is the meaning of mishneh, like a doubling, and similarly 'and it shall be mishneh'; it is mishneh to the king there. Mishneh to the king is an epithet of HaShem, also it is from the root of shenayim, as I have explained. Now this verse explains that 'and in the seventh year you shall let him go free' is at the beginning of the year; also there is proof from 'the year of release' and from 'the day of the sabbath.'" "<b>And bless you.</b> Future tense, not past, for there is no difference between them except by reason of context."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The citation 'the day of the sabbath' is ambiguous; rendered literally as it stands in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:38.076416170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}